WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.686
A carrier can look excellent in a vial, then fail at

00:00:04.686 --> 00:00:08.764
the nebulizer. That is the question behind inhaled dexamethasone formulations.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.941
My master's research examines nonionic niosomes and proniosomes that form

00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:19.681
vesicles upon hydration. Their membranes include Span sixty and cholesterol.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.855
Changing membrane packing could alter a vesicle's response to stress.

00:00:24.855 --> 00:00:29.509
This packing diagram is a formulation hypothesis, not measured morphology.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.386
Before aerosol testing, the samples need size distributions,

00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:38.572
surface charge, drug content, and chemical compatibility measurements.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.456
Microscopy gives a separate view of vesicle structure. These

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:48.711
images come from thesis progress materials, not simulated microscopy.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.615
Drug calibration supports accurate quantitation. Linearity alone cannot tell

00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:59.030
us whether medicine will reach the lung after nebulization.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.823
Air-jet and vibrating-mesh nebulizers make aerosols differently. Each

00:01:04.823 --> 00:01:09.447
device may impose distinct mechanical stresses on nanocarriers.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.114
Those stresses can change vesicle size or cause

00:01:14.114 --> 00:01:18.027
leakage. Measurements before and after aerosolization are essential.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.903
Aerodynamic particle size matters. Fine particle fraction and mass

00:01:24.903 --> 00:01:29.606
median aerodynamic diameter describe aerosol performance, not clinical efficacy.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.494
These comparisons are internal thesis-progress observations. They are

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:38.252
exploratory and have not been independently peer-reviewed.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.727
Aerosol performance is only one gate. Release behavior and

00:01:44.727 --> 00:01:49.255
biological response must also be examined before clinical translation.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.513
Will the medicine survive the nebulizer? The answer depends on formulation

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:58.826
and device together. A promising carrier is not yet a treatment.
